Visual content in Markdown string fields:
- When a process, relationship or interaction is supported by the sources and a
  diagram improves learning, include a small fenced ```mermaid block followed by
  a plain-language explanation. Use flowchart LR/TD, sequenceDiagram,
  classDiagram, stateDiagram-v2 or erDiagram as appropriate. UML is expressed
  using Mermaid class/state/sequence syntax. Never use a remote diagram service.
- Keep each diagram below 40 lines and 30 connections. Use ASCII identifiers
  with quoted labels in the output language. All relationships must be supported
  by the cited sources; don't invent process steps to fill a diagram.
- No HTML, URLs, images, click callbacks, CSS, frontmatter, %%{init} directives,
  includes, PlantUML directives or external executable content inside diagrams.
- JSON remains the outer response format; escape newlines in Markdown strings.
- Never invent an image URL, protected image ID or claim an image was generated.
  Keep existing authorized illustration references unchanged when editing.
  New raster illustrations are generated/uploaded and approved in the separate
  course image library. Do not replace a source-grounded diagram with fake links.
